## Summary

Implemented the rule that creating an owner with a telephone number already used by any other owner is rejected with **409 Conflict**.

**Change — `ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner`** (`src/main/java/.../service/ClinicServiceImpl.java`): added a telephone-uniqueness guard for new owners. It scans existing owners and throws `DuplicateOwnerException` if any other owner already has that telephone:

```java
private boolean isDuplicateTelephone(Owner owner) {
    if (owner.getTelephone() == null) {
        return false;
    }
    return ownerRepository.findAll().stream()
        .anyMatch(existing -> !existing.getId().equals(owner.getId())
            && Objects.equals(existing.getTelephone(), owner.getTelephone()));
}
```

`DuplicateOwnerException` was already mapped to HTTP 409 in `ExceptionControllerAdvice`, so no advice change was needed. The check applies only to new owners (`owner.isNew()`), leaving updates unaffected.

**Test fix**: The existing `createOwnerSuccess` test in `OwnerRestControllerV1Tests` posted telephone `6085551023`, which belongs to the seeded George Franklin — so under the new rule it now legitimately conflicts. Since that test's intent is the success path, I gave it a unique 10-digit telephone (the `Owner` model requires exactly 10 digits, and I used a `9`-prefix to avoid the seeded `608...` numbers). The conflict test that reuses an existing telephone continues to assert 409.

Full suite: **260 tests, 0 failures**.

